      "explanation": "<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 31 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyimcup4/60cf2cb6-94cd-4862-a9e6-5b1fdaf4cdc1/82cc9700-4042-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimcupc.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>(i) Mono-bromination of substituted methyl on 1-methylcyclohex-1-ene.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimfp39/ca49027e-826a-49a4-8