1lyimjijl.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 31 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyimjijk/e748e61d-24c0-43dd-8a38-54b8f2df7003/3c11ca00-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimjijl.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>C-3 is optically active on bromine substitution and gives two optically active isomers.</p>\n\n<p>(iii) Mono-bromination of C-4 carbon :</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimlo57/0f1543b3-43b7-4791-8ffc-cd02055216c8/7803b4b0-4043-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimlo58.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-con