vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 31 English Explanation 8\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyimwqnv/297fb096-2652-44be-96d6-74a85de0d4c6/abdc4cb0-4044-11ef-971a-4de20b2d5d2d/file-jaoe38c1lyimwqnw.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>C-2 is optically active on mono-bromination and gives two optically active isomers. \n<br><br>So, maximum number of possible isomers are 13.</p>"
